    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s roster today, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) stand out as the pillars of our offensive strategy. **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a plus matchup against Javier (5.16 xERA), and despite the park factor drag, his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) makes him our highest-projected asset for run production. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is primed for a massive outing; the confluence of a +16% park adjustment and the favorable right-handed matchup against Baz allows him to slot into the 2-hole with an elite efficiency profile. **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **JJ Bleday** (66.17) also emerge as strong starts, with **JJ Bleday** specifically benefiting from the highest SP skill advantage (+19%) of the day, helping to mitigate the inherent risk of his lower position in the batting order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.89), who narrowly missed the cut. While his potential for stolen bases remains a massive asset in our 5x5 format, the negative platoon adjustment against Bennett forces him into a marginal scoring tier, effectively keeping him on the pine in favor of the higher-ceiling profiles of **Justin Crawford** and **Gavin Sheets**. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** (56.88) and **Zack Gelof** (58.69) represent our \"safe\" plays; both face tough pitching assignments\u2014Imanaga and Javier, respectively\u2014but their solidified roles in the heart of their orders keep them above our benching threshold.\n\nLooking ahead, we must keep a watchful eye on **Bryce Harper** (64.81), whose projection remains bolstered by an excellent 0.389 xwOBA, though the matchup against Leahy lacks the explosive upside found elsewhere in the lineup. Our overall strategy hinges on capitalizing on the SP skill disparities present in today's slate, particularly where we hold significant platoon advantages. We are holding **Daulton Varsho**, **Braden Montgomery**, and **Tyler Freeman** 